    <div class="principles-grid">
      <div class="principle-card">
        <h3>Sub-one-second load.</h3>
        <p>Every sample above loads in under a second on mobile. That's what it looks like when there's no WordPress overhead.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-card">
        <h3>95&ndash;100 PageSpeed.</h3>
        <p>Custom code, optimized images, and no tracking bloat mean Google PageSpeed scores sit in the 95&ndash;100 range by default.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-card">
        <h3>Mobile-first layout.</h3>
        <p>Designed for the phone first, then expanded for tablet and desktop. Because 70%+ of visitors will be on a small screen.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-card">
        <h3>Built for SEO.</h3>
        <p>Clean heading hierarchy, local business schema, fast Core Web Vitals; all baked in. Not bolted on after the fact.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-card">
        <h3>WCAG 2.2 AA accessible.</h3>
        <p>Real contrast ratios, real focus rings, real keyboard navigation. Accessibility isn't a plugin we turn on.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-card">
        <h3>Conversion-focused.</h3>
        <p>Every page has a clear next step; call, book, quote, or email. The design isn't art; it's a working business tool.</p>
